---
interface Props {
  standaloneProject?: "digital-ink" | "edinburgh-map";
}

const { standaloneProject } = Astro.props;

// CHOICE: Digital Ink now has one canonical presentation at /dink/.
// Keep the retired drawer source available for a reversible cleanup, but never render it.
const showLegacyDigitalInkDrawer = false;
---

<div 
  id="project-drawer" 
  data-drawer 
  class:list={["drawer-root", { "drawer-root--standalone": Boolean(standaloneProject) }]}
  aria-hidden={standaloneProject ? "false" : "true"}
>
  <!-- Digital Ink Panel -->
  {showLegacyDigitalInkDrawer && (!standaloneProject || standaloneProject === "digital-ink") && (
  <div 
    data-drawer-panel="digital-ink" 
    data-direction="left"
    class:list={["drawer-panel di-theme", { "is-active": standaloneProject === "digital-ink" }]}
    role={standaloneProject ? undefined : "dialog"}
    aria-modal={standaloneProject ? undefined : "true"}
    aria-label="Digital Ink project details"
  >
    <div class="drawer-scroll">
      {!standaloneProject && <button type="button" data-drawer-close class="drawer-close-x hidden lg:flex" aria-label="Close">×</button>}
      <section class="di-panel di-body overflow-x-clip">
        <!-- Q888:SECTION_START id="di-header" -->
        <div class="pt-32 sm:pt-36 pb-16" style="padding-left: var(--drawer-pad); padding-right: var(--drawer-pad);" data-di-reveal-section>
          <div class="mx-auto">
            <h1 class="di-headline uppercase font-medium tracking-[-0.045em] leading-[0.88] text-[clamp(4rem,9vw,10.5rem)] text-zinc-50">
              DIGITAL INK
            </h1>

            <p class="mt-7 max-w-[70ch] font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed tracking-wide text-zinc-400">
              EARTH RECORD: An iPad art application and post-digital medium created
              in Edinburgh by Alexander Sestakovs / Q888. Released in 2026.
            </p>
            
            <p class="mt-8 mx-auto text-[clamp(1.9rem,3vw,3.4rem)] leading-[1.12] text-zinc-200">
              Digital Ink is a post-digital artistic medium defined by deliberate scarcity. Conceived as an antidote to the frictionless reproducibility of traditional digital tools, it treats the digital canvas as a strictly finite resource. By compressing an entire photograph into a single, irreducible pixel, the project returns the "aura" of authenticity to the digital realm—where every brushstroke carries the weight of a sacrificed memory.
            </p>

            <p class="mt-8 mx-auto text-[clamp(1.3rem,1.5vw,1.6rem)] leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
              Digital Ink turns the smallest unit of digital creation into something with weight:
              <span class="di-tagline-key">one image → one Smart Ink Drop (1×1)</span>
            </p>

            <div class="di-mono mt-10 text-lg sm:text-xl text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              <div>SYSTEM_STATUS: APPROVED · PLATFORM: iPadOS (iPad-only)</div>
              <div>STATUS: AVAILABLE NOW</div>
              <div>ROLE: Concept · Product Design · UX · SwiftUI</div>
              <div>YEAR: 2025–2026</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Q888:SECTION_END id="di-header" -->

        <!-- IMAGE 1 -->
        <div class="full-bleed">
          <div class="aspect-video w-full bg-zinc-900/60">
            <img src="/images/DigitalInk_Ipad_kn.webp" alt="Digital Ink on iPad" class="h-full w-full object-cover" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" />
          </div>
          <div class="di-img-label">APP_VIEW · iPadOS · DRAWING ENGINE</div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION DIVIDER 1 -->
        <div class="di-section-divider" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 600 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
            <line x1="0" y1="16" x2="240" y2="16" stroke="rgba(91,156,246,0.18)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
            <g transform="translate(262, 4)">
              <rect x="0" y="0" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.6)"/>
              <rect x="10" y="0" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.15)"/>
              <rect x="20" y="0" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
              <rect x="0" y="10" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.15)"/>
              <rect x="10" y="10" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.35)"/>
              <rect x="20" y="10" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.15)"/>
              <rect x="0" y="20" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
              <rect x="10" y="20" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.15)"/>
              <rect x="20" y="20" width="8" height="8" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.6)"/>
            </g>
            <line x1="318" y1="16" x2="600" y2="16" stroke="rgba(91,156,246,0.18)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <!-- Q888:SECTION_START id="di-philosophy" -->
        <div class="py-16" style="padding-left: var(--drawer-pad); padding-right: var(--drawer-pad);" data-di-reveal-section>
          <div class="mx-auto">
            <div class="di-eyebrow">// MEDIUM &amp; PHILOSOPHY</div>
            <h2 class="di-h2">Philosophy &amp; Experience</h2>
            <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
              <p>
                Digital Ink challenges the disposable nature of infinite digital tools. In an age where we can undo endlessly and create without consequence, this app asks: what if software imposed physical constraints? Through strict rules of conservation, each pixel becomes a finite material—much like paint in a tube. When you draw, you're not just arranging colors; you are placing an indexical trace of a real-world photograph onto a canvas. The inability to duplicate or summon pixels from nothing turns the act of digital creation into a deliberate, sculptural process where each mark is a weighty commitment.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Q888:SECTION_END id="di-philosophy" -->

        <!-- IMAGE 2 -->
        <div class="py-2" style="padding-left: var(--drawer-pad); padding-right: var(--drawer-pad);">
          <div class="di-reveal aspect-[4/5] sm:aspect-video w-full bg-transparent relative overflow-hidden" data-di-reveal="image2">
            <!-- Base (aligned right, not stretched) -->
            <img
              src="/images/screen.webp"
              alt="Digital Ink canvas (base)"
              class="di-reveal-base absolute inset-y-0 right-0 h-[100%] sm:h-[90%] w-auto top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 object-contain z-10"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              width="800"
              height="600"
            />

            <!-- Overlay (aligned right, not stretched) -->
            <img
              src="/images/screen_overlay.webp"
              alt="Digital Ink canvas (overlay)"
              class="di-reveal-overlay absolute inset-y-0 right-0 h-[100%] sm:h-[90%] w-auto top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 object-contain z-20"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              width="800"
              height="600"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="di-img-label">CANVAS_STATE · HOVER TO REVEAL OVERLAY</div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION DIVIDER 2 -->
        <div class="di-section-divider" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 600 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
            <line x1="0" y1="16" x2="248" y2="16" stroke="rgba(91,156,246,0.18)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
            <g transform="translate(268, 8)">
              <rect x="0" y="0" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
              <rect x="8" y="0" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.5)"/>
              <rect x="16" y="0" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
              <rect x="0" y="8" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.5)"/>
              <rect x="8" y="8" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.9)"/>
              <rect x="16" y="8" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.5)"/>
              <rect x="0" y="16" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
              <rect x="8" y="16" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.5)"/>
              <rect x="16" y="16" width="6" height="6" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
            </g>
            <line x1="314" y1="16" x2="600" y2="16" stroke="rgba(91,156,246,0.18)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <!-- Q888:SECTION_START id="di-innovation" -->
        <div class="py-16" style="padding-left: var(--drawer-pad); padding-right: var(--drawer-pad);" data-di-reveal-section>
          <div class="mx-auto">
            <div class="di-eyebrow">// CONCEPT &amp; INNOVATION</div>
            <h2 class="di-h2">Innovation Beyond Traditional Drawing Apps</h2>
            <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
              <p>
                Unlike Procreate or Adobe Fresco—which optimize for speed and abundance—Digital Ink introduces intentional constraints to give each action significance. The core innovation lies in its approach to digital authenticity: it achieves the rigorous scarcity of blockchain-based art, but deliberately eschews financialization. There are no tokens, no public ledgers, and no speculative mechanics. Instead, cryptographic hashing serves purely as an artistic mechanism to ensure that each pixel remains a provably unique, untamperable archive of its source photograph. It is a system that is provenance-rich but value-agnostic.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <!-- Q888:SECTION_END id="di-innovation" -->

        <!-- IMAGE 3 -->
        <div class="py-8" style="padding-left: var(--drawer-pad); padding-right: var(--drawer-pad);">
          <div class="di-reveal aspect-video w-full bg-transparent relative overflow-hidden" data-di-reveal="image3">
            <!-- Base image -->
            <img
              src="/images/memory.webp"
              alt="Digital Ink memory (base)"
              class="di-reveal-base absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-contain z-10"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              width="800"
              height="600"
            />

            <!-- Overlay image -->
            <img
              src="/images/memory_overlay.webp"
              alt="Digital Ink memory (overlay)"
              class="di-reveal-overlay absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-contain z-20"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              width="800"
              height="600"
            />

            <!-- Fog quote text -->
            <div class="di-fog-text absolute right-0 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 z-15 text-left pointer-events-none">
              <p class="text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,5rem)] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em] leading-[1.1] text-zinc-200/40 blur-[1.5px]" style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; text-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(255,255,255,0.15);">
                I REMEMBER …<br/>being many pixels…
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="di-img-label">MEMORY_VIEW · PIXEL BIOGRAPHY SYSTEM</div>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION DIVIDER 3 -->
        <div class="di-section-divider" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 600 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
            <line x1="0" y1="16" x2="220" y2="16" stroke="rgba(91,156,246,0.18)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
            <g transform="translate(240, 6)">
              <rect x="0" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.6)"/>
              <rect x="7" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.3)"/>
              <rect x="14" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.15)"/>
              <rect x="21" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
              <rect x="28" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.04)"/>
              <rect x="35" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.02)"/>
              <rect x="42" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.04)"/>
              <rect x="49" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
              <rect x="56" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.15)"/>
              <rect x="63" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.3)"/>
              <rect x="70" y="0" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.6)"/>
              <rect x="7" y="7" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.15)"/>
              <rect x="35" y="7" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.6)"/>
              <rect x="63" y="7" width="5" height="5" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.15)"/>
            </g>
            <line x1="360" y1="16" x2="600" y2="16" stroke="rgba(91,156,246,0.18)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <!-- Q888:SECTION_START id="di-details" -->
        <div class="py-16 pb-32" style="padding-left: var(--drawer-pad); padding-right: var(--drawer-pad);">
          <div class="mx-auto">

            <!-- Systems Aesthetic -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// SYSTEMS AESTHETIC</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Three Phases of Engagement</h2>
              <p class="mt-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
                Digital Ink operates on a conceptual three-state machine. First, the <strong>Drop Machine (Extraction)</strong> permanently consumes an imported photograph, downscaling it into a singular SmartInk pixel with cryptographic metadata. Second, the <strong>Canvas (Creation)</strong> enforces strict conservation laws; pixels are spent from your inventory and placed onto a fixed grid without layering. Finally, <strong>Biography Mode (Reflection)</strong> allows viewers to inspect any pixel on a completed canvas, revealing the hidden archival history, semantic context, and origin photograph that powers that tiny dot of color.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Concept-Driven Architecture -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// LOCAL-FIRST</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Concept-Driven Architecture</h2>
              <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
                <p>
                  Every technical decision reinforces the project's philosophy. Built as a native iPadOS app with Core Data SQLite, Digital Ink operates entirely offline. This local-first architecture ensures that true ownership of the art resides fully with the user, mirroring the self-contained nature of a physical art studio. AI and Vision frameworks are utilized minimally and locally for semantic indexing—augmenting the artist's ability to search their inventory without offloading the creative act to an algorithm or risking data privacy.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Exhibition Value -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// INSTALLATION</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Exhibition Value</h2>
              <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
                <p>
                  In a gallery context, Digital Ink transforms from a personal tool into an interactive "system-as-artwork." The application itself becomes an installation where visitors can submit their own photographs to a communal Extraction Kiosk. The resulting pixels feed a shared Canvas where audiences collectively navigate scarcity. Crucially, the final artworks invite deep discovery; viewers can tap the digital paintings to unpack the "archive of memories" embedded in each pixel, making the invisible assumptions of digital creation visible.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Technical Stack -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// STACK</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Technical Stack</h2>
              <div class="di-stack-grid mt-8">
                <div class="di-stack-row">
                  <span class="di-stack-key">FRONTEND</span>
                  <span class="di-stack-val">Swift · SwiftUI · Core Data</span>
                </div>
                <div class="di-stack-row">
                  <span class="di-stack-key">AI / ML</span>
                  <span class="di-stack-val">Apple Vision Framework · GPT-4o API</span>
                </div>
                <div class="di-stack-row">
                  <span class="di-stack-key">BACKEND</span>
                  <span class="di-stack-val">Cloudflare Durable Objects · StoreKit 2</span>
                </div>
                <div class="di-stack-row">
                  <span class="di-stack-key">PLATFORM</span>
                  <span class="di-stack-val">iPadOS — native iPad app</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Development Journey -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// DEVELOPMENT JOURNEY</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Development Journey</h2>
              <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
                <p>
                  As solo developer and designer, I architected every aspect of Digital Ink—from philosophical concept to production deployment.
                  The gesture system required deep study of iOS touch handling to match the polish users expect from tools like Procreate.
                  Implementing server-verified purchases demanded careful security architecture to prevent token fraud while maintaining smooth
                  user experience. The AI integration pipeline needed optimization to balance poetic output quality with performance constraints on-device.
                </p>
                <p>
                  The project launched successfully on the App Store on January 12, 2026, delivering the complete MVP feature set:
                  drawing engine, import system, metadata tracking, in-app purchases, and gallery functionality.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- SECTION DIVIDER 4 -->
            <div class="di-section-divider" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 600 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
                <line x1="0" y1="16" x2="255" y2="16" stroke="rgba(91,156,246,0.18)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
                <g transform="translate(271, 5)">
                  <rect x="0" y="0" width="7" height="7" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
                  <rect x="9" y="0" width="7" height="7" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.25)"/>
                  <rect x="18" y="0" width="7" height="7" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
                  <rect x="9" y="9" width="7" height="7" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.7)"/>
                  <rect x="0" y="18" width="7" height="7" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
                  <rect x="9" y="18" width="7" height="7" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.25)"/>
                  <rect x="18" y="18" width="7" height="7" fill="rgba(91,156,246,0.08)"/>
                </g>
                <line x1="320" y1="16" x2="600" y2="16" stroke="rgba(91,156,246,0.18)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
              </svg>
            </div>

            <!-- Artistic & Cultural Implications -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// CULTURAL POSITION</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Artistic &amp; Cultural Implications</h2>
              <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
                <p>
                  Digital Ink proposes a new form of pixel-based authorship where art becomes a system of resonance and memory, not just visual beauty.
                  Ownership of ink drops ties directly to emotional experiences—imported dream images, meaningful photographs, AI-generated collaborations.
                  Each drawing becomes ritual rather than routine, transforming digital matter with conscious intent. This opens possibilities for symbolic
                  storytelling where the meaning behind each pixel matters as much as its color.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Future Development Roadmap -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// ROADMAP</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Future Development Roadmap</h2>
              <p class="mt-8 text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-400">
                Digital Ink is designed as a platform for expansion into new creative territories:
              </p>
              <div class="di-roadmap-grid mt-10">
                <div class="di-roadmap-card">
                  <span class="di-card-num">01</span>
                  <h3 class="di-card-title">Cloud Sync &amp; Cross-Device</h3>
                  <p class="di-card-body">Long-term ink history synchronized across devices, allowing artists to see how their ink pools evolve over months and years.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="di-roadmap-card">
                  <span class="di-card-num">02</span>
                  <h3 class="di-card-title">Ink Biographies</h3>
                  <p class="di-card-body">Detailed timeline views showing how individual pixels traveled through multiple artworks, creating visual genealogies of creative decisions.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="di-roadmap-card">
                  <span class="di-card-num">03</span>
                  <h3 class="di-card-title">AI Memory Reconstruction</h3>
                  <p class="di-card-body">Smart Inks that speak through AI-powered image reconstruction. Using original image descriptions and accumulated usage history, the system generates impressions from your digital ink memories.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="di-roadmap-card">
                  <span class="di-card-num">04</span>
                  <h3 class="di-card-title">Collaborative Features</h3>
                  <p class="di-card-body">Shared ink pools for co-creation, ink trading between artists, and community-driven symbolic protocols across shared mythologies.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Physical-Digital Hybrid -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// PHYSICAL × DIGITAL</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Physical-Digital Hybrid: Sticker &amp; Skin System</h2>
              <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
                <p>
                  Digital Ink bridges physical and digital realms through limited-edition collectible stickers that unlock app enhancements.
                  Each physical sticker purchase includes a unique digital patch code, creating tangible connection between physical art objects
                  and digital creative tools.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Aura Sticker System -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// AURA SYSTEM</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Aura Sticker System</h2>
              <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
                <p>Each sticker functions as a digital artifact carrying specific aura properties that enhance app functionality:</p>
                <ul class="di-bullet-list">
                  <li>Expands ink capacity beyond the baseline 1,000 Smart Inks</li>
                  <li>Example: <span class="text-zinc-100">"Overpriced Knight"</span> sticker grants +8.88% ink on top of the 1,000 Smart Ink limit</li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                  This system transforms stickers from passive collectibles into functional upgrades while maintaining the core philosophy of meaningful constraints.
                  Limited physical production ensures genuine scarcity, and each sticker's aura is carefully balanced to enhance—not overwhelm—the intentional
                  creative experience.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Premium Cosmetic System -->
            <div class="di-detail-section" data-di-reveal-section>
              <div class="di-eyebrow">// COSMETICS</div>
              <h2 class="di-h2">Premium Cosmetic System: Luxurious Lux</h2>
              <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 mx-auto text-2xl sm:text-3xl leading-[1.55] text-zinc-300">
                <p>
                  For collectors seeking pure aesthetic prestige, Digital Ink offers premium cosmetic upgrades that provide zero gameplay advantage
                  but maximum visual impact.
                </p>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="di-sub-h3">Luxurious Lux Skin features include</h3>
                  <ul class="di-bullet-list mt-4">
                    <li>Full golden/pearlescent UI transformation with subtle shimmer animations</li>
                    <li>Exclusive loading sequences with custom messaging</li>
                    <li>Canvas edge glow effects and refined visual flourishes</li>
                    <li>Premium audio feedback for interactions</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <p>
                  This approach mirrors successful cosmetic systems in gaming and creative software, where optional prestige items support ongoing development
                  while preserving core functionality for all users.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Collectible Strategy -->
